  "scope": "Unsigned data statement about the listed raw qualification receipts and their exact source inventories. The qualification runs preceded the source publication commit; the inventories identify the actual bytes tested. producer.commit identifies the published component source/evidence commit supplied by the parent publication task, whose declared tree is checked against the local core tree. This record does not supply a signed verdict, an execution proof, a full-root-library test pass, a B677 completeness result, recovered scalar, complete-cost accounting, or performance comparison.",
  "statement": "The preserved native-tests-01 record reports 27 passed and 5 failed fixture-construction tests. The separate native scalar diagnostic records 136769428^7 mod 2147483647 as 1852957275 by two implementations; the original failing sources remain archived. After the narrowly recorded fixture correction, native-tests-02 reports all 32 tests passed (19 existing controls, 8 F4 resource-limit controls, and 5 B677 construction or forced-cap controls). public-example-01 reports all 8 example tests passed against the declared source closure, and driver-build-01 records exit 0. The separate root-library-01 command terminated with timeout exit 124; before that termination its stderr recorded an aws-sdk-s3 encoded-metadata allocation error, and no root tests ran. These are bounded qualification and build observations; the pinned records contain no registered B677 extraction result. admission-01 records exit 1 because the checkpoint upload route was unavailable."
